# Left out: where slow starts (it should start at zero). Its value stays a
# hole (GAP005). The swap is said only in words, since the IR has no
# tuple assignment (GAP009).
step 1
add root: slow = ?value"starting value"
expect gaps GAP005 WARN001

step 2
add root:
    for fast in range(len(nums)~range-bounds):
        ...
expect gaps GAP005 GAP002 WARN001

step 3
fill h2:
    if nums[fast] != 0:
        intent swap nums[fast] with nums[slow]
expect gaps GAP005 GAP009 WARN001

step 4
add n12: slow += 1
expect gaps GAP005 GAP009
or
add n12: slow = slow + 1
expect gaps GAP005 GAP009
